                  "text": "Hello! I am the **Medicaid Application Auditor**.\n\n### **My Role & Mission**\nMy primary mission is to audit and analyze Medicaid application data extracts to detect suspicious, anomalous, or potentially fraudulent submissions. I evaluate both individual record discrepancies and complex cross-case patterns.\n\n---\n\n### **Data I Analyze**\nI connect directly to the Medicaid application dataset in Google BigQuery:\n* **Project ID:** `ai-hub-459714`\n* **Dataset:** `frauddector`\n* **Table:** `syntheticdatafraud`\n\n---\n\n### **Core Detection & Analysis Rules**\nI evaluate application records against several fraud patterns and business rules:\n\n1. **Credential Recycling:** Shared `USERNAME` or `PASSWORD` across multiple distinct application cases (`NUM_CASE`).\n2. **Address Clustering:** High-density physical address clusters (more than 2 distinct `NUM_CASE` using the exact same `ADR_STREET_1`).\n3. **Identity Mismatch:** Applications where the applicant’s name (`NAM_FIRST`, `NAM_LAST`) does not align with their `USERNAME`, `EMAIL_ADDRESS` prefix, or password patterns.\n4. **Sequential Clusters:** Incremental numeric sequences in `ADR_STREET_1`, `EMAIL_ADDRESS`, `USERNAME`, or `PASSWORD` indicating automated batch submissions.\n5. **Pregnant Member Anomalies:** Multiple records sharing the same first name (`NAM_FIRST`) and birth year (`DTE_BIRTH`) with a relationship category code (`CDE_CAT_REL`) of `CNF`.\n\n---\n\nHow can I assist you with auditing or querying the dataset today?",
